>	1)  How does one bless or enchant an item?  It is simple to enchant
>	    weapons and armor, but how about other items?

You can only bless other items, not enchant them. Try #dipping them
into holy water.

>	2)  How can one sell items to shopkeepers?  When I talk to them, all
>	    they ever do is !@#%^!@#$ about shoplifters.

Just drop any items in a shop.

>	3)  I've heard about being able to determine the nature of an item (be
>	    (blessed, cursed or uncursed) with an altar.  How is this done?
>	    And does it need to be a similarly aligned to ones character?

Drop the object on the altar. There will be an amber flash if the object
is blessed, and a black flash if cursed.
If you drop water on an altar, it will get holy/normal/unholy water
immediately depending on the altar's alignment.

>	4)  How can one train a pet?

Throw food at it as soon as it's done something useful. In my opinion,
this doesn't work very well, however, and i prefer to leave pets on
the first level if i can't polymorph them into a dragon, Olog-Hai, Lich
or other real useful monster.

>	5)  I hear about all these interesting places (Hell, Memory Vaults,
>	    etc), but cannot seem to locate them.  I've been down to the 25th
>	    level of the dungeon and haven't seen anything out of the ordinary
>	    besides a ghost level...

Hell is in the deep levels, and it should be real near it if you reached level
25. Just keep going down.
Magic memory vaults may appear on any level, and you know there is one on
yours if you hear the footsteps of a guard on patrol or someone counting
money. If you find an 'ad ae?arn?m' scribbling on a floor, search, and you will
find a secret door. Search again, and you will find a corridor.
Walk in it, and you will be teleported into a vault. But take a pick-axe
or some means to teleport with you, or you'll never get out with your money.


